# A Dockerfile is read by a Linux shell, and the shell in the container has no
# idea what a carriage return is. Checked out with CRLF (which is the default on
# this machine), every line continuation in the fixture picks up a stray \r and
# the script it writes gets a shebang no kernel will honour. Keep them LF
# whatever the checkout does.
src-tauri/tests/fixtures/** text eol=lf
